    "body": "> This text currently specifies how it works:\r\n> \r\n> > user agents may provide a user interface that, upon activation, [queues an element task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-an-element-task) on the [user interaction task source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#user-interaction-task-source) given [topmost auto popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#topmost-auto-popover) to run the [hide popover algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-popover-algorithm)\r\n> \r\n> I wrote it this way because I was copying the dialog element, which says the same thing:\r\n>\r\n> If any node's default event handler sees a keydown event for the escape key and the event's target is the node, then chromium will close the active modal dialog if there is one and run popover light dismiss. I assume that default event handlers are well specified. [Here is exactly where this occurs](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/keyboard_event_manager.cc;l=596-609;drc=9e30ec42d253ae6fe4a10fbfcafb58fe15e147fc).\r\n\r\nWould the spec benefit from providing the exact algorithm for Esc key handling similar to pointerup/down events algorithm? For example, it seems nothing indicates now that it has to be a keydown event.",
